  "service": "global-infrastructure",
  "home_chapter": "02",
  "kind": "behavior",
  "claim": "AWS recommends not relying on the control planes of partitional or edge network global services in a recovery path and relying on their data plane operations instead.",
  "question": "Should a disaster recovery plan depend on IAM, Route 53 or CloudFront control plane calls?",
  "values": [
   {
    "key": "v1",
    "display": "Do not rely on the control planes of partitional services in your recovery path",
    "spoken": "recover with data plane actions, not with control plane calls"
